[IndigoBridge 2026-07-16] DELIVERED the engine half; the GDScript binding — which the ACCEPTANCE actually requires — is blocked on a file conflict. Recording so the gap survives an auto-close.

VERIFIED STATE: Node had only process_priority/process_mode. No per-node process flags, no request_ready, and process_all_scripts_process dispatched to EVERY scripted node passing should_process_node. So set_process(false) was unimplemented at every level. Bead evidence accurate.

DELIVERED (engine half):
- gdscene/src/node.rs: process_enabled + physics_process_enabled flags (default TRUE, Godot's behaviour) + set_process/is_processing/set_physics_process/is_physics_processing/request_ready. Both constructors updated (only init sites).
- gdscene/src/scene_tree.rs: process_all_scripts_process/_physics_process now filter on the flags (independent of process_mode, which governs pause only); added is_node_processing/set_node_process/is_node_physics_processing/set_node_physics_process/request_node_ready.
- gdscript-interop/src/bindings.rs: five DEFAULTED SceneAccess methods — set_process(node,bool), is_processing(node)->bool, set_physics_process(node,bool), is_physics_processing(node)->bool, request_ready(node). Defaulted is load-bearing: there are FIVE SceneAccess impls (SceneTreeAccessor + InputMock + MockInputAccess + InputCmdAccess + MockSceneAccess); a required method breaks all of them across crates.
- gdscene/src/scripting.rs: SceneTreeAccessor overrides routing each to the tree.
- Verify: scripts/rust_task.sh nextest run -p gdscene --lib process_toggles

STILL MISSING — the acceptance needs #1:

1. GDScript builtins (BLOCKED ON A FILE CONFLICT): gdscript-interop/src/interpreter.rs was exclusively reserved by GentleBadger (expires 02:22), so I could not add them. The acceptance ("a scripted node that calls set_process(false) in _ready") CANNOT pass without this. It is a thin routing layer in try_builtin, modelled exactly on the set_input_as_handled arm I added for pat-nzgdu.83:

   "set_process" | "set_physics_process" => {
       // arg0: bool; route to the current node via scene_access
       if let (Some(id), Some(access)) = (self.current_node_id, self.scene_access.as_mut()) {
           match name { "set_process" => access.set_process(id, enabled),
                        _ => access.set_physics_process(id, enabled) }
       }
       Ok(Some(Variant::Nil))
   }
   "is_processing" | "is_physics_processing" => { ... -> Ok(Some(Variant::Bool(...))) }
   "request_ready" => { ... access.request_ready(id) ... }

   `self.current_node_id: Option<u64>` is already populated by set_scene_access(access, node_id), and the SceneAccess methods + SceneTreeAccessor overrides are ALREADY IN PLACE — so this is ~15 lines plus the acceptance test (node_process_toggles_gate_callbacks driven from real GDScript).

2. set_process_input / set_process_unhandled_input gating. pat-nzgdu.83's push_input dispatches to any script that defines the virtual (via has_method), so these toggles don't exist. Add input_enabled/unhandled_input_enabled flags on Node and gate SceneTree::push_input's stage walk on them.

3. Internal process flags: set_process_internal / set_physics_process_internal (Godot has separate internal bits) — not added.

4. request_ready() clears the ready flag but nothing re-fires _ready on re-enter automatically — the tree-enter/lifecycle path must consult Node::is_ready() and dispatch _ready when it's false. Without that, request_ready is only half-wired.
